"機能する制御可能なキャラクターにチェイスカメラと複数のアニメーションを追加し"
"ました。次は何が必要でしょうか？"

#: 3D/assets/character_controller.md
msgid ""
"If you're familiar with Godot's 3D orientation, you'll also notice that the "
"character is facing the **+Z** direction, which is backwards. Select the {{< "
"gd-icon Skeleton3D >}}`Skeleton3D` node and set its **Y** **Rotation** to "
"`180` to correct this."
msgstr ""
"```json\n"
"\"If you're familiar with Godot's 3D orientation, you'll also notice that "
"the character is facing the **+Z** direction, which is backwards. Select the "
"{{< gd-icon Skeleton3D >}}`Skeleton3D` node and set its **Y** Rotation to "
"`180` to correct this.\","

#: 3D/assets/character_controller.md
msgid ""
"First, we want to transition to the \"Jump_Start\" animation by setting "
"`jumping = true`. This triggers the transition in the state machine."
msgstr ""
"まず、「ジャンプ開始」アニメーションに移行するために `jumping = true` を設定"
"します。これにより状態機械での遷移がトリガーされます。"

#: 3D/assets/character_controller.md
msgid ""
"There are many ways to handle a 3D camera that follows the player. For this "
"example, we'll use a {{< gd-icon SpringArm3D >}}`SpringArm3D` as the camera "
"\"mount\"."
msgstr ""
"プレイヤーを追従する3Dカメラの実装方法には様々なものがあります。この例では、"
"カメラ用マウントとして `{{< gd-icon SpringArm3D >}}`SpringArm3D` を採用しま"
"す。"

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid "We have several options to consider for designing our level:"
msgstr ""
"私たちのレベル設計には、以下のいくつかの選択肢を検討する必要があります："

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid ""
"The \"wall_doorway_scaffold_door\" is the mesh that we want to rotate.\n"
"We want to be able to open the door in either direction, so we're going to "
"create two animations. Both of them rotate the door's **Y** rotation by "
"`90°`, but \"open+\" opens in the **+Z** direction and \"open-\" does the "
"opposite. This way, when the player interacts with the door, we can open it "
"away from them, no matter which side they're on."
msgstr ""
"「wall_doorway_scaffold_door」は、回転させたいメッシュです。\n"
"ドアを両方向に開閉できるようにするため、2つのアニメーションを作成します。どち"
"らのアニメーションもドアの**Y軸**周りの回転を`90°`変更しますが、「open+」は"
"**+Z方向**に、「open-」はその逆方向に開きます。これにより、プレイヤーがドアに"
"触れたとき、どの側に立っていても外側に開くようになります。"

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid ""
"You can even use Godot's built-in [Blender support](https://"
"docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/assets_pipeline/"
"importing_scenes.html#importing-blend-files-directly-within-godot) to make "
"this even easier. Changes to your `.blend` file will instantly appear in "
"your Godot project."
msgstr ""
"Godotの組み込み[Blenderサポート](https://docs.godotengine.org/ja/stable/"
"tutorials/assets_pipeline/importing_scenes.html#importing-blend-files-"
"directly-within-godot)を活用すれば、さらに簡単に連携できます。`.blend`ファイ"
"ルに変更を加えると、その変更が即座にGodotプロジェクトに反映されます。"

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can turn on grid snapping in the editor and just drag "
"scenes directly from the **FileSystem** tab to place them. This has the "
"advantage of being more flexible than `GridMap`, although a bit more manual "
"in how you go about placing objects."
msgstr ""
"また、エディターでグリッドスナップを有効化し、直接 **ファイルシステム** タブ"
"からシーンをドラッグ＆ドロップして配置することも可能です。この方法は "
"`GridMap` よりも柔軟性に優れていますが、オブジェクトの配置手順がやや煩雑にな"
"るという側面があります。"

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid ""
"1. The GridMap functionality in Godot is fairly rudimentary (especially "
"compared to its 2D equivalent) and hasn't been updated in some time.\n"
"1. Placement is limited to a fixed grid layout, so you don't have as much "
"control over how your meshes are placed."
msgstr ""
"1. Godot のグリッドマップ機能は比較的基本的なもので（特に2D版と比較すると）、"
"長い間更新されていません。\n"
"1. 配置は固定グリッドレイアウトに限定されるため、メッシュの配置自由度が限られ"
"ています。"

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid "#### GridMap"
msgstr "#### グリッドマップ"

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid ""
"Using the built-in {{< gd-icon GridMap >}}`GridMap` node allows you to "
"layout meshes in a grid in the editor. It's similar in concept to the 2D {{< "
"gd-icon TileMap >}}`TileMap` node, though with less functionality."
msgstr ""
"組み込みの `{{< gd-icon GridMap >}}GridMap` ノードを使用すると、エディター上"
"でメッシュをグリッド状に配置できます。この概念は2D用の `{{< gd-icon TileMap "
">}}TileMap` ノードと似ていますが、機能性はやや限られています。"

#: 3D/assets/level_design.md
msgid ""
"Add an {{< gd-icon AnimationPlayer >}}`AnimationPlayer` node, which we'll "
