#: animation/animation_state_machine.md
msgid ""
"When you select an animation, the tree will follow the connected path from "
"the current node to the destination. However, in the configuration above, if "
"you play \"attack2\" you won't see \"attack1\" along the way. That's because "
"the default \"switch mode\" for a connection is \"Immediate\". Click the "
"\"Move/select\" button and then click on the connection from \"attack1\" to "
"\"attack2\". In the Inspector, change _Switch Mode_ to \"AtEnd\". Do the "
"same with \"attack2\" to \"idle\". The connection icon changes from <i "
"class=\"fas fa-play\"></i> to <i class=\"fas fa-step-forward\"></i>."
msgstr ""

#: animation/animation_state_machine.md
msgid ""
"But now the animation stops on \"attack2\". On its connection, set the _Auto "
"Advance_ property to \"On\". This will make the tree go back to \"idle\" "
"after playing both animations. Note that the connection icon turns green to "
"show this."
msgstr ""

