#: physics/Godot3_KYN_rigidbody1.md
msgid ""
"Reset the linear velocity to `(0, 0)`. Now what if you want to be able to "
"toss\n"
"the ball? You should never set a rigid body's velocity or position manually "
"-\n"
"remember, these are simulating \"real-world\" style physics. In the real "
"world,\n"
"objects can't instantly jump from place to place or from a standstill to a "
"high\n"
"speed. If you try and do so, the physics engine will resist it, and "
"unexpected\n"
"movement can occur. Instead, we must apply forces which create an "
"acceleration in a certain\n"
"direction (also known as Newton's Second Law). Godot physics objects work "
"in\n"
"the same way."
msgstr ""

