"records\n"
"the location of the click. When the button is released, we find the vector "
"from\n"
"the click point to the release point and use that to apply the impulse "
"(multiplying\n"
"by `5` to scale it up). `apply_impulse()` also takes an `offset` as its "
"first\n"
"parameter. This lets you \"hit\" the body off center, if you wish. For "
"instance,\n"
"try setting it to `Vector2(25, 0)` and you'll add some spin to the ball "
"when\n"
"it's launched."
