msgid ""
"var speed = 250\n"
"var velocity = Vector2()"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"if position.y > 600:\n"
"        get_tree().reload_current_scene()\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"> **Note:** A {{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}`KinematicBody2D` can be "
"affected by gravity and other forces, but you must calculate the movement in "
"code. The physics engine will not move a {{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}"
"`KinematicBody2D`."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"One of the most powerful but frequently misunderstood collision features in "
"Godot is the collision layer system. This system allows you to build up very "
"complex interactions between a variety of objects. The key concepts are "
"_layers_ and _masks_. Each collision object has 32 different physics layers "
"it can interact with."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"> **NOTE:** `move_and_slide()` automatically calculates frame-based movement "
"using `delta`. Do _not_ multiply your velocity vector by `delta` before "
"passing it to `move_and_slide()`."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"For this example, we'll assume you have a level made of StaticBody2D "
"objects. They can be any shape and size. In the sample project, we're using "
"a TileMap to lay out the level, but for the purposes of this demo, they "
"could just as well be individual static bodies."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"This also allows you to implement other features like wall jumps using "
"`is_on_wall()`,\n"
"for example."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "## Collision shapes"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "- {{< gd-icon StaticBody2D >}}`StaticBody2D`"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"export (int) var run_speed\n"
"export (int) var jump_speed\n"
"export (int) var gravity"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"This is the minimum velocity when standing on a slope. This prevents a body "
"from sliding down a slope when standing still."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
