"This is the maximum angle before a surface is no longer considered a "
"\"floor\"."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func _physics_process(delta):\n"
"\tget_input()\n"
"\tvar dir = get_global_mouse_position() - global_position\n"
"\t# Don't move if too close to the mouse pointer\n"
"\tif dir.length() > 5:\n"
"\t\trotation = dir.angle()\n"
"\t\tvelocity = move_and_slide(velocity)\n"
"{{< /highlight >}}"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"What if you don't want a sliding collision response? For this example "
"(\"BounceandCollide.tscn\"\n"
"in the sample project), we have a character shooting bullets and we want the "
"bullets to\n"
"bounce off the walls."
msgstr ""

