"enum {IDLE, RUN, JUMP}\n"
"var velocity = Vector2()\n"
"var state\n"
"var anim\n"
"var new_anim"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"When moving a {{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}`KinematicBody2D`, you should "
"not set its `position` directly. Instead, you use the `move_and_collide()` "
"or `move_and_slide()` methods. These methods move the body along a given "
"vector and will instantly stop if a collision is detected with another body. "
"After a {{< gd-icon KinematicBody2D >}}`KinematicBody2D` has collided, any "
"_collision response_ must be coded manually."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"`move_and_slide()` provides a default collision response of sliding the body "
"along the\n"
"collision object. This is useful for a great many game types, and may be all "
"you need\n"
"to get the behavior you want."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid "**Example:**"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
