msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"func shoot():\n"
"\t# \"Muzzle\" is a Position2D placed at the barrel of the gun\n"
"\tvar b = Bullet.instance()\n"
"\tb.start($Muzzle.global_position, rotation)\n"
"\tget_parent().add_child(b)"
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"Using the floor normal allows us to make jumping work, using "
"`is_on_floor()`. This\n"
"function will only return `true` after a `move_and_slide()` collision where "
"the\n"
"colliding body's normal is within 45 degrees of the given floor vector (this "
"can\n"
"be adjusted by setting `floor_max_angle`)."
msgstr ""

#: physics/Godot3_kinematic2d.md
msgid ""
"Anything you do with `move_and_slide()` can also be done with "
"`move_and_collide()`,\n"
"it just might take a little more code. However, as we'll see in the examples "
"below,\n"
"there are cases where `move_and_slide()` isn't the response you want."
msgstr ""

